Some sentences come from Uzbek Wikipedia, which is licensed under CC BY-SA; the pairs keep its share-alike
terms. Other sentences are short excerpts from published books, from copies publicly available on the internet. Each pair's source_id names its source, and
we remove any sentence on request (open an issue in the repository). The pairs in external/ were generated
by Javohir Matniyozov from the tahrirchi/uz-books-v2 collection (labelled MIT on its Hugging Face page).

Exception: multiblimp_uzb.tsv is the Uzbek split of MultiBLiMP 1.0 (Jumelet et al.), included for comparison.
It is not ours and stays under its own licence; see the MultiBLiMP release.

The code in scripts/ is licensed under the MIT licence (../LICENSE).
